*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* calculator-2-match.sno — arithmetic-expression pattern match ONLY, Variant 2:
* ARBNO iteration (the grammar of calculator-2.sno with every semantic action
* stripped).  Whole file in memory, ONE BIG MATCH, zero side effects.  The
* subject is the entire input: a run of newline-terminated expression lines,
* ARBNO(X eol), anchored POS(0)..RPOS(0).
*
* Atoms A (lowercase letters, unsigned ints, parens), signed factors F (unary
* sign chains via *F), terms T ('*' '/'), expressions X ('+' '-').  Where -1
* uses right recursion in T/X, this variant folds the operator chains with
* ARBNO — the fullscan-safe iterative shape (calculator-2.sno's header
* explains why the literal Gimpel left-recursive form stack-overflows on every
* engine).  Language recognized is identical to calculator-1-match; the ARBNO
* form removes the alternative re-parse of F that the right-recursive form
* pays, so the two make a clean A/B on how the pattern engine handles deferred
* recursion vs bounded iteration.  Shares calculator.input / calculator-gen.py.
* Run: sbl -b calculator-2-match.sno < calculator.input
*      snobol4 -b -f -d 8m -P 4m -S 4m calculator-2-match.sno < calculator.input
*      scrip --run calculator-2-match.sno < calculator.input
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        V              =  ANY('abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz')
        I              =  SPAN('0123456789')
        A              =  V | I | '(' *X ')'
        F              =  A | ANY('+-') *F
        T              =  F ARBNO(ANY('*/') F)
        X              =  T ARBNO(ANY('+-') T)
        eol            =  CHAR(10)
        C              =  POS(0) ARBNO(X eol) RPOS(0)
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        &TRIM          =  0
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  ONE READ — SPITBOL raw mode: -f0 attaches stdin, -r sets raw record length;
*  newlines come back in-string, short read at EOF (manual, file processing)
        INPUT(.INPUT, 9, '[-f0 -r4000000]')
        src            =  INPUT                          :F(fail)
        src            C                                 :F(fail)
        OUTPUT         =  'matched bytes=' SIZE(src)      :(END)
fail    OUTPUT         =  'Pattern match failed'
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
END
